   145   * Handle a NX window blocked event.  This handler is called when we
   146   * receive the BLOCKED message meaning that there are no further pending
   147   * actions on the window.  It is now safe to delete the window.
   148   *
   149   * This is handled by sending a message to the start window thread (vs just
   150   * calling the destructors) because in the case where an application
   151   * destroys itself (because of pressing the stop button), then we need to
   152   * unwind and get out of the application logic before destroying all of its
   153   * objects.
   154   *
   155   * @param arg - User provided argument (see nx_block or nxtk_block)
   156   */
   157
   158  void CWindowMessenger::handleBlockedEvent(FAR void *arg)
